  "counting_note": "The cumulative ledger counts all named local/global instances as well as definitions and theorems. Contributor narrative counts sometimes exclude instances; the exhaustive source-derived axiom ledger is authoritative.",
  "actual_theorem": {
    "setting": "The ORIGINAL periodic four-dimensional SU(2) Wilson law rho with coefficient beta multiplying the unnormalized fundamental real trace. The period n is even and greater than one; beta is in[0,1/36). Tests are real continuous functions on the actual compact configuration space.",
    "operators": "Q_c is the actual conditional-expectation projection resampling all links of geometric color c with the exterior fixed. P=(1/8) sum_c Q_c is one uniform random-color update. Product-law equality, stationarity, reversibility and projection residual identities are proved from the original action.",
    "variance_factorization": "Var_rho(F) <= [sum_{c=1}^8 integral |F-Q_cF|^2 d rho] / (1-36 beta).",
    "auxiliary_gap": "E_P(F,F) >= (1-36 beta)/8 Var_rho(F). The rate is independent of lattice volume, but beta<1/36 is essential for a positive lower bound.",
    "all_step_decay": "For centered continuous F, |integral F P^k F d rho| <= 2*#Links*||F||_infinity^2*q^k, q=1-(1-36 beta)/8. Finite coordinate oscillation budgets also give expectation convergence from every initial configuration.",
    "prefactor_removal": "Reversibility converts even moments to true L2 iterate norms. Weighted convexity of these squared norms removes arbitrary finite observable-dependent prefactors from the one-step gap. No global variance or spectral-norm bound is assumed.",
    "measure_identity": "A Haar-preserving measurable coordinate equivalence pushes the literal stateAction Gibbs law to the original Wilson law, with both inverse measure transport and arbitrary real integral equality. The final variance theorem explicitly names the original law.",
    "completion_scope": "The actual Poincare theorem is for continuous real observables and their actual L2 norms. A separate completed L2 update representation is not claimed. A generic symmetric-operator dense-moment theorem is separately proved."
  },
  "closed_connections": [
    "Actual affected plaquettes equal four-link incidence; shared-plaquette multiplicities have row sum<=18, including period two.",
    "Actual one-coordinate Wilson staple changes give C_ab=2 beta multiplicity. Its row and column sums are<=36 beta.",
    "Continuous bounded-test influence is extended to every measurable event using proved regularity/continuous approximation, then bound to actual Wilson laws.",
    "Actual product-law expectation comparison is proved by marginal Fubini and finite telescoping, without assuming a global mixing estimate or measurable coupling.",
    "The conditional/Dirac product kernel is exactly the true block-resampling operator, as measures and expectations.",
    "The resulting collective oscillation and moment bounds imply the actual volume-independent continuous variance inequality."
  ],
  "natural_next_route_not_formalized": {
    "locality": "Prove P sends a continuous observable supported on A to its one-layer plaquette-neighbor enlargement, and <F,(I-P)G>_rho=0 for disjoint link supports. The latter follows naturally from product conditionals within a color, but is not yet a new formal theorem.",
    "clustering": "With graph distance d(A,B), these identities would telescope Cov(F,G)=<P^d(F-rhoF),G-rhoG>. The auxiliary L2 decay would then give |Cov(F,G)|<=q^d sqrt(VarF VarG). This uses support propagation, not an identification of auxiliary update time with Euclidean separation.",
    "cylinder": "Construct a rectangular open time cylinder of arbitrary length L at fixed spatial period. For the standard Wilson action with full spatial terms at both endpoints, temporal-link integration gives b(U0) product_t K(Ut,U(t+1)) b(UL), b=exp(-beta V/2). An explicitly half-weighted endpoint action instead gives product K and boundary vector1, matching the existing constant-boundary open-chain construction. Keep these conventions distinct.",
    "two_time_dictionary": "For standard full-endpoint Wilson action, prove moments equal <b,T^s M_F T^k M_G T^t b>/<b,T^(s+k+t)b>, b=exp(-beta V/2). For explicitly half-weighted endpoints replace b by1. Extend local geometry/color bounds uniformly to the open cylinder; endpoint coefficients are no larger than the bulk coefficient.",
    "vacuum_passage": "At fixed spatial cutoff, take the two boundary lengths to infinity using the already constructed positive simple vacuum. The predicted limit is <psi F,(T/lambda0)^k psi G>. Uniform cylinder clustering could then give a volume-uniform ORIGINAL transfer bound in the same strong-coupling range, without a trace-class premise.",
    "limits": "The isotropic periodic n^4 theorem alone does not establish this fixed-spatial-period temporal limit. The cylinder/locality/dictionary remain missing. Even completing them would not give the weak-coupling trajectory beta(a)->infinity, continuum survival or the Clay theorem."
  },
  "independent_review": "Two agents independently checked the variance constant, factor-eight cancellation, actual probability-law identification, reversible-moment prefactor removal and distinction from physical transfer time. At beta=0 a one-color observable saturates the auxiliary gap1/8, consistent with the normalization.",
