  "remaining": [
    "The physical mass gap remains unproved. The new actual variance factorization is for the four-dimensional Euclidean SU2 Wilson law, with 0<=beta<1/36 and even period n>1, and its auxiliary random-color heat bath. It is not a functional inequality for the three-dimensional squared-ground law or the original transfer clock.",
    "Prove physical-time collective contraction or Var_pi_a(f)<=C/a E_P_a(f) for the actual squared-ground law and ORIGINAL full transfer, with C uniform in cutoff/volume along an independently identified physical trajectory. The strong-coupling bound does not extend to beta(a)->infinity.",
    "Construct the original open rectangular time-cylinder action and exact two-time transfer dictionary at fixed spatial period, including half-spatial endpoint weights and integrated temporal gauge links. Extend incidence/color/update locality uniformly to this geometry; the isotropic periodic n^4 law alone does not provide this fixed-spatial-volume temporal limit.",
    "Prove support propagation for the actual color update and vanishing cross Dirichlet pairing on disjoint supports; combine with the new auxiliary contraction to obtain actual Euclidean graph-distance clustering. Then pass through the exact cylinder/vacuum dictionary. This is a proposed proof route, not an already formal physical-transfer gap.",
    "The actual Poincare theorem is for real continuous observables with their actual L2 norms and conditional projection residuals. A separate completed L2 update representation and all-domain extension are not asserted. Generic dense-test moment contraction is proved and can support that extension.",
    "Construct a nonzero renormalized four-dimensional continuum with physical coupling/normalization identification, surviving finite-energy source overlap, uniform all-order mixed-source Schwartz bounds, common-domain fields, cyclicity, Poincare covariance, joint forward-cone spectrum and locality for every compact simple gauge group.",
    "All twelve full Clay requirements remain open. No full-root build or Clay certificate is claimed."
  ],
